@@ -140,6 +140,20 @@ changes (where available).
 
 ## UI/UX Improvements
 
+- The Android fork adds Lighttable and Darkroom workspaces, a thumbnail grid,
+  native history sidebar, folding inspector and filmstrip. Module presets,
+  instance copying/renaming and selective style creation reuse native processing.
+
+- The Android fork saves originals, native XMP processing and tool assets in a
+  persistent photo workspace. It adds named recovery snapshots, session-history
+  navigation, original darktable .dtstyle import/create/apply/export, a pinned
+  comparison image and an optional preview RGB histogram.
+
+- The Android fork adds a resizable photo/inspector workspace, a searchable tool
+  catalog, preview zoom, landscape panes and Russian interface resources. Numeric
+  drafts survive tool switching. Opening another edited photo and stopping a
+  session now explain when current edits will be discarded.
+
 - Added back and forward navigation in collections, with user-assignable
   shortcuts. Navigation remembers collection rules and thumbnail scroll
   positions for up to 32 visits during the current session.
@@ -670,6 +684,9 @@ changes (where available).
 
 ## Bug Fixes
 
+- The Android fork rejects photo drags and multitouch as mask/tone selections,
+  uses a searchable sheet for lens profiles and translates lens status in Russian.
+
 - Fixed bands of slightly wrong colors in images demosaiced with AMaZE
   whose height or width is 1 to 15 pixels more than a multiple of 128.
 
