+# Darkroom Mobile: Android workspace fork
+
+Based on `togekk39/darktable-android` master
+`ae4139bdf18a5c39f71c24f1fb3eab320c139cc9` (2026-11-26).
+The processing source lock identifies darktable
+`1c4eaea9df6dbe8336449ca297acbb0120d8e968`.
+This is an unofficial development fork, independent of Spektrafilm.
+Version 0.3.0 adds native desktop XMP and .dtstyle integration; see the
+[desktop comparison](DESKTOP_PARITY.md). The older 0.2.1 audit is historical.
+
+## Workspace
+
+- A fixed top toolbar contains Open, Undo, Redo and Export.
+- The photograph is above its inspector in portrait and beside it in landscape.
+  Drag the separator to resize them. Accessibility progress actions resize the
+  same separator; activating it restores the default ratio. Landscape retains at
+  least 280 dp for controls and 240 dp for the photo.
+- The preview supports pinch/pan, double-tap zoom/fit, a Fit button and expansion
+  into the inspector area. These transformations never enter the pixel pipeline.
+  Native photo-coordinate tools reset/disable preview zoom so their existing
+  geometry mapping remains valid.
+- Light/Color, Detail/Repair and Geometry/Effects retain the complete original
+  tool inventory. Settings opens a full-height application preferences page.
+- Tap the tool name for a searchable category catalog. The separate search
+  button searches names and parameter labels across all categories. Exact
+  native instance IDs and On/Off states are retained. Navigation never enables
+  a tool or creates a native edit.
+- Parameters retain their original controls, ranges and precise number inputs.
+  Numeric drafts now survive tool switches, full-photo view and saved-state
+  restoration. Blending/parametric masks and drawn/repair masks have labeled
+  expandable sections; nothing is removed or merged.
+- Russian app resources cover every translatable shell string. Tool labels use
+  the original Russian darktable MO catalog. Native IDs, values and the native
+  processing locale are unchanged. The existing languages remain selectable.
+- Opening another edited photo from the editor asks before opening the picker.
+  Cancelling that picker leaves the photo intact. The original engine's Cancel
+  is terminal for the session; stopping an operation with a previous photo now
+  explicitly confirms that it will close the session. Finishing an operation
+  automatically removes an obsolete stop dialog.
+
