+
+## Build with the original processing runtime
+
+The fork does **not** replace native processing algorithms. The engine comes
+byte-for-byte from the checksum-verified upstream APK for the exact source
+revision above. Version 0.3.0 adds one source-built JNI bridge calling the
+original public XMP/style APIs. The APK contains the original 115 engine/runtime
+libraries, that bridge, one independently pinned AndroidX native library and
+830 runtime data files. The module list distinguishes the added bridge from
+the observed original APK inventory; it does not enable optional desktop codecs.
+
+Use JDK 17, Gradle 8.14.4, Android Platform/Build Tools 35 and an official NDK
+providing API 26 AArch64 system stubs. The official wrapper JAR and distribution checksum are included; see
+[README.md](README.md). From the repository root:
+
+```sh
+curl --fail --location \
+  https://github.com/togekk39/darktable-android/releases/download/dev-latest/darktable-android-dev-ae4139b.apk \
+  --output /tmp/darktable-upstream-ae4139b.apk
+python3 android/tools/prepare-upstream-runtime.py \
+  --apk /tmp/darktable-upstream-ae4139b.apk --ndk /absolute/path/to/ndk \
+  --output /absolute/path/to/new-runtime-stage
+cd android
+./gradlew :app:testDevDebugUnitTest :app:testDevReleaseUnitTest \
+  :app:assembleDevRelease :app:lintDevRelease \
+  -PdarktableRuntimeStage=/absolute/path/to/new-runtime-stage
+```
+
+The recovery tool requires upstream APK SHA-256
+`be88cc10e2b9cd9b17ae73eecb49c105ab001d6d0f8a05e2512e5eeb65010d8a`.
+It preserves original native bytes and compiles the small desktop JNI bridge
+with the supplied NDK. It validates the API 26 system stubs separately
+without mixing another NDK's C++/OpenMP runtimes into the APK's original closure.
+The original staging and final APK verifiers check all runtime hashes and ELF
+metadata. For a native source build, use the upstream
+[engine bootstrap instructions](../mobile/dependencies/ENGINE_BOOTSTRAP.md) and
+supply that matching stage instead.
+
+Normal builds now require an explicit engine stage. The old engine-disabled
+route requires `-PdarktableDependencyProbe=true`; it remains explicitly unable
+to open/process photos. An unsigned or dependency-only APK is not this delivery.
+The development release uses application ID `design.komarpunk.darkroom.dev`,
+version 0.3.0/code 4, and a development signing key. It installs beside the
+original author's app. Keep a persistent production key before distributing
+updates beyond this development build.
+
+## Validation boundary
+
+The original revision passed 189 Android/JVM tests, 39 runtime producer/verifier
+checks, four host C adapter tests and an engine-enabled debug build locally.
+The new workspace adds host-executed Compose checks for exact numeric dispatch,
+draft retention, fullscreen/resize, disabled instances, search, narrow Russian
+screens, landscape limits, zoom, import/cancellation and confirmation controls.
+Captures under `app/build/reports/mobile-workspace` render the actual Compose
+view tree with a sample image. They are UI fixtures, not RAW-engine screenshots.
+
+The [functional audit](FUNCTION_AUDIT.md) records the 0.2.1 results: 289 host
+Android/JVM checks per variant, the native engine suite and real NEF/RAF processing
+through the original JNI bridge on Linux. Robolectric itself does not execute
+the native engine. The APK retains the original ARM64 native bytes; the audit's
+Linux engine build is separate. There was no attached Android phone/emulator.
+Every camera, every control's pixel effect, OEM document providers, performance
+and process-death behavior remain outside the verified scope. Preview/export
+differences were measured and are explicitly documented in the audit.
+
+Photo originals, XMP processing, immutable tool assets, reference images and
+snapshots now persist in app-private storage. Session Undo starts again after
+reopening; a native XMP project is not the serialized mobile Undo ring. Real
+.dtstyle import/create/apply/export is available. External share intents create
+a separate saved photo project. Full built-in module preset browsing, several
+automatic pickers, linked liquify/freehand mask workflows and optional codecs
+retain the port's coverage limits. See
+[control coverage](../mobile/CONTROL_PARITY.md). Existing scalar/dedicated
+controls were not removed to conceal these gaps.
+
+## GitHub fork
+
+The local branch is `feat/mobile-workspace`. Creating a GitHub fork through the
+connected integration returned HTTP 403 `Resource not accessible by integration`.
+No application source changes were pushed to the author's repository or to
+Spektrakrill's main branch. Separate delivery branches and prereleases in
+Spektrakrill distribute the APK, matching source ZIP, patch and audit evidence;
+they do not integrate this editor into Spektrafilm. GitHub's automatic Source
+code archives for those tags are not the Darkroom source ZIP.
+Create the fork in the owning GitHub account, grant the connector access to it,
+and then push the reviewed branch to that new repository. Never force-push an
+existing fork or substitute the author's `master` remote as a writable target.
