diff --git a/android/desktop-bridge/ABI.md b/android/desktop-bridge/ABI.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b43a44f613975b2369701bdb0aae3a0f3bdc4d07
--- /dev/null
+++ b/android/desktop-bridge/ABI.md
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Desktop interop ABI
+
+This bridge uses public C symbols from the pinned darktable source, not a
+private `dt_mobile_session` or `dt_develop_t` memory layout:
+
+- `dt_imgid_t` is `int32_t`: `src/common/darktable.h`.
+- `dt_image_get_id_full_path`: `src/common/image.h`.
+- `dt_exif_xmp_write`: `src/common/exif.h` (`TRUE` means failure).
+- Style creation/import/export/apply/delete: `src/common/styles.h`.
+- Per-module preset enumeration/export: `src/common/presets.h`; only the public
+  `dt_presets_params_t` value record is read. Its opaque parameter buffers are
+  exported by the engine, not interpreted by the bridge.
+- Selective style rows and pixel-mask portability guard: `src/common/styles.h`.
+  Long row selections are chunked before the original fixed SQL buffer limit.
+- Ratings, color labels and tag assignment: `src/common/ratings.h`,
+  `src/common/colorlabels.h`, `src/common/tags.h`.
+
+The declarations retain the exact C ABI of the source revision. Tag assignment
+uses opaque public `GList` pointers, allocated/freed by the runtime's own
+`g_list_append` / `g_list_free`. No list or image-cache struct is dereferenced. All symbols
+are resolved against the verified engine during linking (`--no-undefined`).
+The existing JNI UTF-8 conversion is reused, including rejection of NUL and
+unpaired surrogates. Kotlin executes interop on its single native dispatcher.
+
+Style application writes a native XMP before retiring the old develop context.
+Even on error, the app loads the saved XMP into a replacement context and
+retires the old context before publishing the result. Keeping the runtime alive
+through this handoff avoids reinitializing the desktop global type registry.
+It must never continue rendering an old context against a database altered by
+the public style API. A recovery snapshot retains the
+previous processing. Applying a style starts a fresh mobile Undo session.
+
+Catalog updates use the public cache-aware rating/tag APIs, with internal
+`darktable|` tags preserved and grouping/session Undo disabled. Values and every
+tag are validated before changing image assignments. Native XMP remains the
+durable authority. `NativeCatalog.restore` repairs the pinned importer's comma
+splitting of RDF tags (`src/common/exif.cc:_exif_import_tags`) after opening,
+before checkpoint/export, through the same public tag API. Pixel math is unchanged.
+
+Batch items own a captured XMP and immutable encoder settings. The worker copies
+the retained original to a new scratch path and opens that copy, so importing its
+history cannot mutate the active editor's image ID. Only one item is processed
+at a time, on the existing native dispatcher, while the editor retains a runtime
+user. SHA-256 readback checks the new SAF output before the item is marked done.
+The queue persists; it is not a foreground service and does not promise execution
+after Android kills the process. Interrupted items need explicit retry.
+
+Build a new stage with `android/tools/build-desktop-bridge.py`. The original
+stage is read-only; all original library/data hashes remain identical. The
+new ARM64 library is recorded explicitly in the derived stage manifest and
+the complete stage/APK verifier is run. No binary is patched or renamed.
